From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Default apps: Email

Settings > Apps > Default apps (0021) gets an Email row: the app mail
links open with, a Linux mail app (Thunderbird, Evolution, Geary, ...: one
whose desktop file takes x-scheme-handler/mailto) or a mail website
registered with the browser (navigator.registerProtocolHandler). Until now
mail links went to whichever Linux mail app had been launched last, or did
nothing.

- A Linux app chosen: prefs::kNickelMailApp, which
  GuestOsRegistryService::GetHandler now prefers for mail links (the
  browser's mail links, and links Linux apps hand ChromeOS); the browser's
  mail website, if any, stops being the default; nickel-appd writes it to
  nickelos-mimeapps.list, so Linux apps' xdg-open and the portals go
  straight to the app.
- A website chosen: the browser's protocol handler default, as
  chrome://settings/handlers sets it; Linux apps' mail links come back to
  ChromeOS (nickel-open), which opens the website.
- VmApplicationsService's NickelOpenLink: nickel-open's mail links (the
  website, else a Linux mail app, else Settings > Apps to choose one; a
  tab left open, and a second link blocked by the external protocol
  handler's guard, came with the old way through the browser).
- A mail link a page hands an app loses attach= and attachment=: mail apps
  attach the local files a link names.
- No built-in mail website: ChromeOS predefines Gmail for mailto: (and
  Google Calendar for webcal:), which the Email row showed as the default.

